// @description Biscot1 Synth
// @version 2.29
// @author Lo-lo
// @changelog
//   First ReaPack publication of Biscot1 Synth v2.29.

desc: Biscot1 Synth
// v2.29 TEST Always Auto: Oversampling/AA is permanently Auto; slider1 is intentionally free for a future control.
// v2.28 TEST Zero-DC Composite 5/6/7: extends analytic DC centering to AA Triangle+Pulse; keeps v2.27 Saw+Pulse and Triangle+Saw+Pulse fixes unchanged.
// v2.27 TEST Zero-DC Composite 6/7: removes analytic DC bias from AA Saw+Pulse and Triangle+Saw+Pulse before level makeup/nonlinear output stages.
// v2.26 TEST Runtime Fast Paths: exact/near-exact CPU fast paths for 50% Square mipmap, cached mip selection, normalized table reads and safe mono output processing.
// v2.25 TEST Cold Reset Idle: sleep is keyed from real VCA silence + no held MIDI, then runtime state is atomically returned to cold-init state.
// v2.24 TEST Zero-Work Idle: idle @sample has no branch and writes no outputs; DSP exists only when active.
// v2.23 TEST: reports automatic tail detection to REAPER so a warm silent instance can
// return to host auto-bypass/sleep after its real output tail has ended.
// v2.22 TEST: Cold Idle Return. Once every audible Amp ADSR is fully finished,
// silent Mod/Filter envelope tails are collapsed so the synth returns to true cold sleep.
// v2.21 TEST: deep idle block sleep; MIDI remains live, inactive block-rate pitch/ARP/drift work sleeps.
// Declares no audio input because the instrument never reads input samples, allowing REAPER host-side input optimizations.
// v2.18 TEST MipMap-AA: true oscillator-source band limiting for Triangle/Saw/Pulse.
// Auto uses octave/mip band-limited wavetables at 1x when Ring/Sync are off; rest of synth stays at project rate.
// This is a diagnostic/quality experiment: if foldback remains on a plain primitive wave, it is being created downstream.
// CPU Deep Optimization: conditional oscillator components, static-pitch/filter fast paths,
// sleeping ARP preparation, 1x oscillator fast path, stereo-only routing cleanup and cached output stage.
// Audio engine aligned with the Biscot1 Tracker Core; autonomous MIDI synth, no GMEM.
// v2.20 TEST: Triangle+Saw AA blend retuned: zero-DC, stronger Saw identity, reduced startup click.
// v2.19 TEST: extends mip-mapped source antialiasing to SID combined waves.
// In Auto, combined waves reserve bandwidth before polynomial DAC interaction; Off keeps the original 8-bit SID path.
// Historical v2.17: Oversampling Off/Auto was block-live and independent from MIDI Mode.
// v2.29 removes that selector: Auto is now permanent and slider1 is intentionally unused.
// AA mipmaps stay active at 1x for normal waves; Ring/Sync still select adaptive 2x/4x/8x/16x.
// v2.16: first correction of the Oversampling selector source.
// v2.15: adds independent Upper/Lower Squash controls for each LFO; six new sliders, 190 total.
// v2.11: modular stereo filter. Centered operators use one mono filter; stereo opens only when filtered pan is used.
// v2.10: true idle sleep even with active LFO destinations; only free-running LFO phases advance while silent.
// v1.98: multichannel layout changed to 2 inputs / 10 outputs: Mix 1/2, Op1 3/4, Op2 5/6, Op3 7/8, Filter 9/10.
// v1.97: declares explicit audio input/output pins for correct REAPER pin reporting.
// v1.94: adds the historical SID Voice 3 Off switch: Op3 is muted only from the direct path, while oscillator, envelope, ring, sync and modulation remain active; if Op3 To Filter is On it remains audible through the filter.
// v1.93: adds a fixed SID-style global output stage before Master Volume: subtle model-dependent asymmetric amplifier, external ~16 kHz low-pass and very-low DC blocker. No new sliders.
// v2.00: restores fixed operator Pan after Level and adds per-operator Mod Env Pan Depth before Pitch Mod Depth.
// v2.01: in Chord Allocate, fixed Pan and Mod Env Pan Depth are independent per operator; LFO Pan remains controlled by the Op1 Pan Depths as before.
// v1.96: in Chord Allocate, each LFO Op1 Pan Depth controls all three allocated voices. Outside Chord Allocate, LFO pan depths remain independent.
// v1.92: replaces global Drift with per-operator Note-On Drift controls after the trigger group. In Chord Allocate, Op1 Drift amount controls all three voices.
// v1.91: fixes Note-On Drift using the LJuno rand(2)-1 method and LJuno-style +/-0.5 semitone maximum range.
// v1.90: Drift is sampled independently per operator on Note On, LJuno-style.
 // It no longer moves continuously over time, starts immediately detuned, and removes the per-sample drift random/smoothing path.
 // v1.89: conservative CPU pass; caches drift smoothing and static mode/routing choices outside @sample without changing synthesis equations.
// v1.88: doubles the effective 6581 resonance response as an experiment, while retaining the existing safety clamp below self-oscillation.
// v1.86: doubles the effective 8580 resonance response while keeping 6581 unchanged and retaining a safety clamp below self-oscillation.
// v1.85: adds Filter Input before the filter core for both 8580 and 6581; renames Filter Volume to Filter Output. Defaults preserve the v1.84 sound.

// Biscot SID Composite Lab
// v2.03: restores Op1 as the shared Trigger/Legato control in Chord Allocate; per-operator Pan and Mod Env Pan remain independent.
// v1.77: in Chord Allocate, all three independent arpeggiators read the complete held chord instead of only the single note allocated to each mono voice.
// v1.84: keeps the 6581 filtered output at -12 dB but restores a little more post-filter saturation without changing the level trim.
// v1.83: lowers only the active 6581 filtered output by 12 dB after all filter colour/resonance processing, preserving its character.
// v1.82: lowers the complete 6581 model by 3 dB after level comparison without the filter.
// v1.81: removes the Poly Mode control and all Poly 2 fixed-register allocation code. Chord Allocate keeps its original default voice allocation. Drift remains after Filter Volume.
// v1.79: adds global three-voice pitch Drift; 0 bypasses the drift path, default 0.18.
// v1.78: in Chord Allocate, every incoming chord note feeds all three independent SID Seq memories; each sequence keeps its own clock/step position.
// v1.76: in Chord Allocate, the three arpeggiators are independent (mode, rate, octave range, SID sequence and glide) while the rest of the synth panel continues to follow Op1.
// v1.75: in Chord Allocate, Op1/Op2/Op3 Pitch sliders remain independent while the rest of the synth panel continues to follow Op1.
// v1.74: fixes Op1 Level in Chord Allocate: it is now the real shared VCA level and is no longer cancelled by level-based normalization.
// v1.73: Chord Allocate uses Op1 as the complete master synth panel for all three allocated mono voices; only note/gate/voice state remain independent.
// v1.72: each operator Mod Env can modulate the rate of LFO1, LFO2 or LFO3 with a bipolar depth. Depth 0 bypasses the extra rate calculation.
// v1.70: the former Pitch Env is now the per-operator Mod Env. It directly modulates pitch and PWM with independent bipolar depths; PWM source selectors removed.
// v1.69: PWM envelope modulation per operator adds bipolar Depth and selectable source (Amp ADSR, Filter ADSR, Pitch ADSR).
// v1.68: adds an independent pitch ADSR for each operator. Depth is bipolar +/-48 semitones with 0.01-semitone resolution; controls are physically inserted after Portamento.
// v1.67: 6581 saturation is made more parallel and dynamic: less envelope flattening and less sustain-like swelling, while keeping the dirty colour.
// v1.63: noise LFSR clock raised two octaves while preserving pitch tracking; multichannel routing from v1.62 retained.
// v1.62: multichannel routing changed to Op1 1/2, Op2 3/4, Op3 5/6, filtered bus 7/8 with filtered operators removed from dry.
// v1.61: adds Audio Mode Stereo/Multichannel; global slider order starts with Oversampling, Audio Mode, MIDI, restart/model/volume/noise. Filter Key Follow moved after HP.
// v1.60: adds Filter Key Follow in the filter section and Noise Character as a global SID-style noise blend.
// v1.59: slider order reorganized into four sections: global, three-operator groups, filter, and three LFO strips.
// v1.58: renumbers and compacts sliders so operator/LFO parameters appear in grouped sequential order.
// v1.56: removes the Composite Character slider; 6581 LP+BP+HP three-state lift is lowered by 1 dB.
// v1.55: lowers the closed-cutoff floor a little, especially on 6581 LP, so cutoff 0 catches lower harmonics for basses.
// v1.54: 6581 low-pass resonance presence boosted after the clean core, without reintroducing pre-filter saturation.
// v1.53: 6581 pre-filter drive removed from the resonant path; resonance is cleaner/post-filter so saw stays saw-like.
// v1.51: 6581 resonance hybridized: core feedback kept below oscillation, extra clean resonant presence added after the stable core.
// v1.50: 6581 resonance reworked at the feedback/core level: cleaner resonant bite, no free self-oscillation gate.
// v1.48: safer 6581 resonance top end and note/envelope-following filter silence gate so the dirty model does not keep singing after note-off.
// v1.47: 6581 three-mode filter has more perceived level; 6581/8580 resonance scale is slightly stronger but still clamped against self-oscillation.
// v1.46: expands LFO PWM Depth slider ranges to +/-1.5 so LFO PWM can cover a wider pulse-width sweep.
// v1.45: removes LFO Ring/Sync depth sliders and related @sample gate logic. LFOs now modulate cutoff, pitch, PWM and level only; Ring/Sync remain manual SID switches.
// v1.42: removes user-facing High Pitch Guard and its per-sample guard path; Oversampling is now only Off/Auto and Auto handles high-register cleanup.
// v1.41: Sample Hold/Smooth Random rate fixed: no extra double phase; delay fade-in and One Shot Length retained from v1.40.
// v1.57: renamed Hard Restart labels: SID Player -> Env Reset, Aggressive -> Full Reset. Logic unchanged.
// v1.39: LFO Trigger/One Shot now follows the same Trigger/Legato decision as the Op1/Filter ADSR: Trigger restarts every note; Legato restarts only on the first non-legato note.
// v1.38: CPU pass. LFO strips sleep completely when all their depths are zero; LFO increments/smoothing/delay coefficients are cached outside @sample. Oversampling slider reduced to Off/Auto.
// v1.37: adds three independent BPM-synced LFO strips with direct depths for cutoff, Op pitch/PWM/level. Rate: 1=bar, 4=beat, 8=eighth, 16=sixteenth, up to 512; below 1 gives multi-bar cycles.
// v1.36: replaces the global Legato Mode with per-operator Mode Trigger sliders. Removes the separate Pulse Width sliders from the UI; PWM Extended is now the only visible pulse-width control.
// v1.35: Chord Allocate now uses Op1 as the shared timbre/VCA panel for all three mono voices, while notes/legato remain per voice. Adds per-voice MIDI pitch-bend range 0..96 semitones.
// v1.33: stronger oscillator/ring anti-aliasing. Adds 8x/16x oversampling choices, lets Auto reach 8x on dangerous high notes/ring-sync, and restores a little high-register energy after BLEP so very high notes do not disappear.
// v1.30: extended PWM remapped as an extreme SID-style duty range; Op Semitone is now continuous Master Tone +/-96 semitones with 0.01 step. Fine Cent remains separate.
// v1.29: removed redundant Op3 Ghost Audio Mode. Op3 Level=0 now acts as the SID-style silent modulator path.
//       Ring/sync modulators keep their oscillators running through another operator's release, so ring does not collapse to a clean oscillator tail.
// v1.24: ARP glide depth now uses an LSH-2-style independent coefficient per operator; it no longer requires operator Portamento to be above zero.
// v1.26: reinserted SID Seq Dynamic Length as ARP mode 1, with clock-only note entry and release-transparent playback.
// v1.25: in ARP mode, note-ons update the arp pool only; oscillator pitch changes only on arp clock steps, never immediately.
// v1.24: ARP glide depth is now independent from normal operator portamento.
// v1.23: ARP is note-off transparent: while an arp mode is active, note-offs do not shrink or transpose the latched arp; it keeps cycling until idle.
// v1.22: release ARP is now transparent: it freezes the arpeggio base note/root during release so note-off order cannot transpose the arp.
// v1.21: fixed release ARP latch. Note-off no longer overwrites the release latch with the last single note; release keeps the full arpeggio set.
// v1.20: added per-operator ARP glide depth. ARP frequency steps can now be rounded with portamento-style curves, LSH-2 style.
// v1.19: replaced experimental SID Seq with the proven LSH-2 ARP2 frequency engine, cloned independently for Op1/Op2/Op3.
// v1.18: arp keeps running during envelope release using a per-operator release latch, like LSH-2.
// v1.13: added SID-player style frequency arpeggiator per operator. It changes oscillator pitch/frequency without MIDI note retrigger, separately for Op1/Op2/Op3.
// v1.12: SID-correct oscillator topology for ring modulation and sync. Ring affects the triangle component only; sync resets on the modulator accumulator MSB rising edge.
// v1.7: moved 6581 level compensation from global oscillator output to the filtered path only.
// v1.6: fixed held-note stack so repeated same-note Note On events are not collapsed; prevents short skipped notes.
// v1.5: stronger 6581 Dirtier make-up gain to better match perceived level with 8580 Clearer.
// v1.4: virtual negative cutoff range, bipolar filter envelope behavior, stronger musical resonance and +3 dB composite-character make-up gain.
// v1.3: added dedicated filter ADSR, mono legato/retrigger behavior, held-note return and per-operator portamento.
// v1.2: added output gain compensation for 6581 Dirtier model.
// v1.1: softer musical 6581 baseline and safer non self-oscillating resonance.
// v1.0: LP/BP/HP all Off now bypasses the filter instead of muting routed operators.
// v0.9: fixed ADSR with explicit Attack, Decay, Sustain and Release states.
// v0.8: sliders reordered as a matrix for easier testing without Lua.
// v0.7: filter study update: 6581 R4 low-pass never fully disappears; 8580 R5 low-pass can close hard and has cleaner resonance.
// Ring and sync now follow the SID ring/sync chain: Op3 -> Op1, Op1 -> Op2, Op2 -> Op3.
// v0.6: SID-style filter routing: Op1/Op2/Op3 can enter filter separately; LP/BP/HP are independent summed switches.
// v0.5: cleaner 8580 baseline, homogeneous operators for chord tests.
// v0.4: starts with only Op1 audible.
// Op2 and Op3 are silent until their levels are raised, but can still act as sync/ring references.
// v0.3: corrected architecture.
// This is NOT an 8-voice synth.
// It is one SID-like block: 3 monophonic operators/voices.
// Modes:
// 0 = all 3 operators follow the same MIDI note
// 1 = first 3 held notes are assigned to operators 1, 2, 3
// 2 = MIDI channels 1, 2, 3 directly control operators 1, 2, 3

// --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// v1.72: Mod Env LFO Rate Target/Depth controls are physically inserted after Pitch/PWM modulation depths.
// v1.68: three independent pitch envelopes, one per operator, inserted after Portamento and before Arp controls.
// v1.67: reduces 6581 sustain-like compression by blending post-filter and final clipping with the clean signal.
// v1.65: moves Op1/Op2/Op3 PWM sliders before the operator Attack sliders and renumbers references accordingly.
in_pin:none

out_pin:Mix Left
out_pin:Mix Right
out_pin:Op1 Left
out_pin:Op1 Right
out_pin:Op2 Left
out_pin:Op2 Right
out_pin:Op3 Left
out_pin:Op3 Right
out_pin:Filter Left
out_pin:Filter Right

